### Custom Footer
The `footer` slot receives `formId`, `submitting` and `cancel`; the submit button points at the form with `form`, so Enter and a click submit alike.

```vue
<TxModalForm v-model="open" :initial-values="member" @submit="save">
  <template #default="{ model }">…</template>
  <template #footer="{ formId, submitting, cancel }">
    <TxButton variant="danger" :disabled="submitting" @click="remove">Delete</TxButton>
    <TxButton :disabled="submitting" @click="cancel">Cancel</TxButton>
    <TxButton variant="primary" native-type="submit" :form="formId" :loading="submitting">Save</TxButton>
  </template>
</TxModalForm>
```

### Best Practices

- Keep it to a few fields. Use `TxDrawerForm` for long forms, forms that scroll, or forms read against the page.
- Return a promise from `@submit`. Return `false`, throw, or call `setErrors()`, and the dialog stays open.
- Modal forms do not autosave. To save as the user edits, put a `TxForm` with `autosave` in a `TxDrawer`.
- In a custom footer, close with the slot's `cancel`: like Escape, it asks first.
- Outside English, pass `submitText`, `cancelText`, `messages.leaveConfirm`, and `modalProps.closeLabel` to name the close button.

## API Reference

### Props

The `TxForm` props below apply too: the dialog builds `model` from `initialValues`, and `autosave` does not apply.

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|-------------|
| `modelValue` | `boolean` | required | Shows the dialog. Use with `v-model`. |
| `title` | `string` | `''` | Dialog title. |
| `width` | `string` | `'480px'` | Dialog width. |
| `initialValues` | `FormValues` | - | The values the form opens with. Each open edits a copy, so the parent's values change only when the parent changes them. |
| `submitText` | `string` | `'Save'` | Text of the submit button. |
| `cancelText` | `string` | `'Cancel'` | Text of the cancel button. |
| `modalProps` | `Record<string, unknown>` | - | Any other `TxModal` prop, such as `surface` or `fullscreen`. Closing is asked of the form, not of `beforeClose`. |
| `id` | `string` | generated | The form's id, and the prefix of every field id. |
| `rules` | `FormRules` | - | Form-level rules keyed by field path. |
| `schema` | `FormStandardSchema` | - | A Standard Schema v1 validator checked against the whole `model`; issues with no matching field are listed in the error summary. |
| `layout` | `'auto' \| 'side' \| 'stacked' \| 'inline'` | `'auto'` | Field layout. |
| `labelPosition` | `'left' \| 'right' \| 'top'` | - | Older spelling of `layout`. |
| `labelAlign` | `'start' \| 'end'` | `'end'` | Label alignment in the side column. |
| `labelWidth` | `string \| number` | `16em` | Widest the side label column may grow; numbers are in pixels. |
| `requiredMark` | `'asterisk' \| 'optional' \| 'none'` | `'asterisk'` | Marks required fields with an asterisk, optional fields with `messages.optional`, or neither. |
| `validateOn` | `'blur' \| 'submit'` | `'blur'` | When the first message appears: on leaving a changed field, or on the first submit. |
| `messages` | `Partial<FormMessages>` | - | Overrides the built-in text. |
| `size` | `'small' \| 'medium' \| 'large'` | `'medium'` | Size of the controls inside; the dialog width is `width`. |
| `disabled` | `boolean` | `false` | Disables the controls inside that read the form, and blocks submit. |
| `readonly` | `boolean` | `false` | Shows the values as a record: controls can be focused and copied, not changed; no field is marked required. |
| `reconcile` | `FormReconcile` | - | Decides what `model` holds when fetched values reach fields the user changed. |
| `persist` | `boolean \| FormPersistOptions` | `false` | Keeps what the user typed under `id`; `true` takes the defaults. |
| `leaveConfirm` | `FormLeaveConfirm \| false` | host's, then `window.confirm` | Asked before leaving with changes no draft holds; `false` never asks. |
| `onSubmit` | `(values: FormValues, event?: Event) => unknown` | - | Called once every check passes; the dialog stays open until a returned promise settles. `@submit` binds it. |

### Events

| Event | Payload | Description |
|-------|---------|-------------|
| `update:modelValue` | `(value: boolean)` | The dialog opens or closes. |
| `submit-success` | `(values: FormValues)` | The submit went through; the dialog closes next. |
| `validate` | `(valid: boolean)` | As on `TxForm`. |
| `persist-error` | `(error: unknown)` | As on `TxForm`. |

### Slots

| Slot | Props | Description |
|------|-------|-------------|
| `default` | `{ model, dirty, valid, submitting, submitted, errors, rootError }` | The form items. `model` is the copy this open edits. |
| `footer` | `{ formId, submitting, cancel }` | Replaces the cancel and submit buttons. |

### Exposed Methods

| Name | Type | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| `form` | `TxForm \| null` | The form inside while the dialog is open, with every `TxForm` method; `null` while it is closed. |
| `cancel` | `() => Promise<void>` | Closes as Cancel does: the form first asks about changes it would lose. |

## Overview

- Each open builds `model` from a copy of `initialValues` and makes it the baseline. Closing unmounts the form with the dialog, so edits never carry over to the next open.
- When `initialValues` changes while the dialog is open, as when a record finishes loading, it becomes the saved state: untouched fields take the new values, and fields the user changed keep their edits.
- Escape, the mask, the close button and Cancel all go through the form's `confirmLeave()`, which asks only about changes no draft holds. A running submit cannot be closed.
- Escape with focus inside a `TxForm` does not reach this path (see the Modal focus rule), so it asks nothing.
- A submit that goes through emits `submit-success`, then closes.
- The footer sits outside the `<form>`, and the submit button reaches it through `form`: Enter in a field and a click make the same submit with the same checks.

## Technologies

- Built from `TxModal` and `TxForm`, with `beforeClose` wired to the form's `confirmLeave()`. Opening, copying and closing share `form/src/use-overlay-form.ts` with `TxDrawerForm`.
- Source: `packages/tuffex/packages/components/src/modal-form/`.

